    "result_text": "There is a single test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, responding with HTTP 400, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `EnsureRegistrationDateNotFuture.java` \u2014 a function step that reads the request (`@Val OwnerFieldsDto`) and throws when a *supplied* `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`. When the date is omitted it passes through (it defaults to the server date downstream), matching the \"when present\" pattern used by `EnsurePostcodeValidForCity`.\n- `FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 a checked exception carrying the rejected value.\n- `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail` (fields `field`/`rejectedValue`), mirroring `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`.\n- `escalation/....FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `ensureRegistrationDateNotFuture` step between `ensurePostcodeValidForCity` and `resolveRegistrationDate`, so the future-date check runs on the raw supplied value before the business-day rolling logic.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate: 2999-01-01`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS.",
